  "result": "I fixed all three problems in `src/queue.js`, and `npm test` passes with 6 of 6 tests, including 4 new regression tests. I didn't run the new tests against the old code, so I haven't confirmed they fail there.\n\n- **Hang after a failure:** a job that rejected never gave its slot back, so the queue stalled. A job that threw synchronously also escaped the queue's handling. Both cases now reject only that job's promise, release the slot and start the next job.\n- **`onIdle()` resolving early:** it only checked that nothing was pending. It now also requires that nothing is running.\n- **One job at a time after `pause()`/`resume()`:** `next()` started at most one job per call. It now loops until every free slot is filled, so `resume()` with concurrency 4 starts four jobs.\n\nThe new tests in `test/queue.test.js` cover a rejecting job, a synchronously throwing job, `onIdle()` waiting for running jobs, and `resume()` filling all slots.",
